WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.940
Every roofing company in Hawaiʻi is looking for good people.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.300
Beachside already has the story.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:11.300
What it needs is a straighter line — from attention to a qualified hire.

00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:15.230
More applicants isn't the same as a better crew.

00:00:15.230 --> 00:00:17.670
The gap isn't effort. It's fit.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.300
Here's the whole line — from first look to the hire.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.090
Discovery.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:28.570
Short videos, a QR code on a truck, a career fair.

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:31.050
All of it points to one place.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.200
Join the Crew.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.800
The culture film, the open positions, the apply button — already part of the website.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:41.570
Then it reaches Tony.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:46.230
Applications arrive, someone screens them, someone follows up.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.590
This is the part we confirm with him.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:56.420
Volume doesn't tell you who can work at height, who can travel between islands, or who will still be here in six months.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.300
That's the opportunity.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:07.800
A Beachside recruitment system: structured questions before the first call, a summary Tony can actually use, and a record of where good people came from.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:10.910
It doesn't replace Tony's judgment.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.490
It gives him better information before the conversation.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.950
The website is already in scope.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:23.710
The system is a separate, optional build — designed around his process, not around software.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.360
A better pipeline of qualified, hire-ready candidates.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:29.460
That's the goal.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.220
What would make this process easier for you?
